SQL> -- Runs AFTER 95_data.sql, deliberately: both assertions below need the seed already in place.
SQL> -- road_admin_reachable is `exists`, which is false against an empty table, so it cannot be
SQL> -- created before the seed grants road.role.grant to road.system_admin. Creating both here also
SQL> -- makes them validate the seed -- a 95_data.sql that produced a violation fails the deploy at
SQL> -- this step (spec-patch-07 section 5.3).
SQL> --
SQL> -- Needs CREATE ASSERTION, granted schema-scoped (not CREATE ANY ASSERTION) by
SQL> -- admin/grant-schema-privileges.sql. See planning/spike-07-1-assertion-support.md.
SQL> 
SQL> -- The invariant is PROVENANCE, not state: road.system_admin legitimately holds road.role.grant,
SQL> -- and calendar_admin legitimately holds events.purge -- both are reserved permissions attached to
SQL> -- roles. What is forbidden is a reserved permission attached BY A SESSION. attached_by is null for
SQL> -- a deploy (no session context to read a principal from) and always non-null for
SQL> -- road_admin_api.attach_permission, which takes it from road_ctx_pkg.principal_id -- so the audit
SQL> -- column carries the rule (spec-patch-07 section 5.1).
SQL> --
SQL> -- COMMA JOIN, NOT ANSI: `JOIN ... ON` is rejected with ORA-08735 inside an ORA-08689 wrapper on
SQL> -- 26ai (spike-07-1 section 3.3). This is not a style choice -- an ANSI rewrite looks like tidying
SQL> -- and fails at deploy time, not review time. Do not "simplify" this to a JOIN.
SQL> --
SQL> -- This is an ASSERTION rather than a BEFORE INSERT trigger on road_role_permissions because the
SQL> -- escalation this guards against is the PARENT table (road_permissions) being updated -- flipping
SQL> -- an existing row's is_reserved to 'Y' out from under an already session-attached grant. A trigger
SQL> -- on the child table would never fire for that case (spike-07-1 section 3.4, row 3).
SQL> create assertion road_reserved_composition check (
  2    not exists (
  3      select 1
  4        from road_role_permissions rp, road_permissions p
  5       where p.permission_name = rp.permission_name
  6         and p.is_reserved = 'Y'
  7         and rp.attached_by is not null
  8    )
  9  );

Assertion ROAD_RESERVED_COMPOSITION created.

Elapsed: 00:00:00.173
SQL> 
SQL> -- Reachability, the other direction. This assertion does NOT cover DELETE -- a `not exists`
SQL> -- predicate cannot be violated by removing a row, so road_reserved_composition does not stop
SQL> -- detaching road.role.grant from road.system_admin, and that would be a lock-out (the role keeps
SQL> -- its holders, so revoke_role's last-administrator guard never fires). Named on the PERMISSION,
SQL> -- not the role, because the invariant is "somebody can still grant roles", not "this particular
SQL> -- role still exists" (spec-patch-07 section 5.3). Together with revoke_role's refusal to remove
SQL> -- the last road.system_admin holder, administration stays reachable from both directions.
SQL> create assertion road_admin_reachable check (
  2    exists (select 1 from road_role_permissions where permission_name = 'road.role.grant')
  3  );

Assertion ROAD_ADMIN_REACHABLE created.

